venv312/

# CI-log captures: put them in .ci-logs/. They are scratch evidence, never
# source, and `git add -A` has swept them into commits four times now
# (win_failure.txt, searchlive_failure.txt, webkit_failure.txt, and
# searchlive2.txt -- which the name pattern below did NOT match).
#
# THE DIRECTORY IS THE GUARD. The `*_failure.txt` pattern is a backstop that
# still catches the three historical names if they recur, but matching on names
# cannot cover a class whose names are invented ad hoc each time: the fourth
# capture was called searchlive2.txt and sailed straight through.
.ci-logs/
*_failure.txt
